        "timestamp": 1773572746,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Who is running Iran? The regime's new strongmen Middle East Issued on: 15/03/2026 - 12:05 In the third week of war, who is leading the country? And to what extent have those still in place been destabilised and weakened by the US and Israeli strikes on the country? A veil of mystery surrounds a man who remains out of sight: Iran's new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei. Another figure, Ali Larijani, meanwhile appeared centre stage at a pro-government demonstration. What role is oil playing in the war in the Middle East and what's at stake? 15/03/2026 Analysis Middle East Gaza hit by strongest sandstorm in over five years 15/03/2026 Middle East Qatar, Kuwait, UAE... Iranian reprisals disrupt daily life across the Gulf 15/03/2026 Middle East Undercover in Iran: How French spies gather Intelligence in the Middle East 15/03/2026 Middle East Israel pounds Beirut, deepening the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon 15/03/2026 Middle East Donald Trump says will open Strait of Hormuz \"one way or another\" 15/03/2026 Middle East Iranian strikes, Hezbollah rockets make regular life in Israel ‘simply impossible’ 14/03/2026 Middle East UN force base in southern Lebanon comes under fire, one peacekeeper wounded 14/03/2026 Middle East US embassy attacked in Baghdad after strikes kill Iran-backed fighters in Iraq 14/03/2026 Middle East"
